vacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mister-M-alt/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-10-18T00:27:07Z","updated_at":"2026-10-18T00:27:07Z","body":"[A10] Ruling on R645-1-F1 (PR #183, head 29f58ad3): F1 stands and is in scope for round 2.\n\nAssignment item 2 says any other length is refused. Its words \"exactly as today\" were wrong: today a body longer than 84 bytes is accepted and echoed at its own length. That also breaks the \"Done when\" line that says the response always uses the 2021 form. Neither IEEE 1722.1-2021 7.4.15.1 / Figure 7-40 nor Milan v1.2 5.4.2.9 defines a longer SET_STREAM_INFO body.\n\nRound-2 contract:\n- only control_data_length 60 and 96 are accepted;\n- every other length is refused as a short body is today: same status, a cdl 96 response, and no offset write;\n- add upper-bound checks at cdl 97 and one longer length, using a valid MSRP_ACC_LAT_VALID template, each with a planted mutant that reopens the gate;\n- update the observed-command record and docs/architecture/06_aecp_engine.md to the same contract.\n\nR645-1-F2 goes to the residue checklist. The round-2 assignment follows R644-1.\n","author_association":"OWNER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Mister-M-alt/protocol-processor-control-plane-avb-milan/issues/comments/6243713960/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Mister-M-alt/protocol-processor-control-plane-avb-milan/issues/comments/6248817225","html_url":"https://github.com/Mister-M-alt/protocol-processor-control-plane-avb-milan/issues/176#issuecomment-6248817225","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Mister-M-alt/protocol-processor-control-plane-avb-milan/issues/176","id":6248817225,"node_id":"IC_kwDOT06kyc8AAAABdHViSQ","user":{"login":"Mister-M-alt","id":161579364,"